<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/app.css">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'><rect width='32' height='32' rx='6' fill='%232563eb'/><text x='16' y='23' font-size='20' text-anchor='middle' fill='white' font-family='system-ui' font-weight='bold'>J</text></svg>">
  <style>
    .setup-nav { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; padding:1rem 0; margin-bottom:2rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
    .setup-nav .logo { font-weight:800; font-size:1.1rem; text-decoration:none; color:var(--text); }
    .setup-nav .logo span { color:#2563eb; }
    .setup-step { display:flex; gap:1.25rem; margin-bottom:2rem; }
    .step-badge { flex-shrink:0; width:2rem; height:2rem; border-radius:50%; background:#2563eb; color:#fff; font-weight:700; font-size:0.9rem; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; margin-top:0.2rem; }
    .step-badge.optional { background:#6b7280; }
    .step-body { flex:1; }
    .step-body h3 { margin:0 0 0.4rem; font-size:1rem; }
    .step-body p { margin:0 0 0.5rem; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem; }
    .step-body code { background:#f4f4f5; padding:0.1em 0.4em; border-radius:3px; font-size:0.875em; }
    .optional-tag { display:inline-block; font-size:0.7rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em; background:#f4f4f5; color:#6b7280; padding:0.1em 0.5em; border-radius:3px; vertical-align:middle; margin-left:0.4rem; }
    .setup-footer { margin-top:3rem; padding-top:1.5rem; border-top:1px solid var(--line); font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--muted); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container" style="max-width:680px; padding:1.5rem 1rem;">

  <nav class="setup-nav">
    <a href="/" class="logo">Just<span>Invoice</span></a>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; font-size:0.875rem;">
      <a href="/login">Log in</a>
      <a href="/signup" style="color:#2563eb; font-weight:600;">Sign up free</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <h1 style="font-size:1.6rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.02em; margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Getting Started</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">Set up JustInvoice in a few minutes. The minimum is: business info + tax + create your first invoice. Stripe is <em>optional</em> — if your clients pay by Interac e-Transfer (most Canadian service businesses), you don't need it at all.</p>

  <!-- Step 1 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Create your account</h3>
      <p>Sign up at <a href="/signup">the signup page</a>. All you need is an email and password — no credit card required to get started.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step 2 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Set up your business info</h3>
      <p>Go to <a href="/settings">Settings</a> and fill in your business name, email, phone, and address. This info appears on every invoice you create.</p>
      <p>Also set your <strong>invoice number prefix</strong> (e.g. <code>INV</code>, <code>ACME</code>) — invoices will be numbered like <code>INV-2025-0001</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step 3 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Configure sales tax <span class="optional-tag">optional</span></h3>
      <p>In <a href="/settings">Settings → Sales tax</a>, enable your tax type (HST, GST, VAT, etc.) and enter the rate as a decimal.</p>
      <p>Common rates: <code>0.05</code> = 5% GST, <code>0.13</code> = 13% Ontario HST, <code>0.20</code> = 20% UK VAT.</p>
      <p>Once enabled, each new invoice will include a tax line automatically. You can also override per-invoice.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step 4 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge optional">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Choose how you want to get paid <span class="optional-tag">recommended</span></h3>
      <p>You have two options. Pick whichever fits your business — you can change this any time in <a href="/settings">Settings → How clients pay you</a>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;"><strong style="color:var(--ink);">Option A — Interac e-Transfer (recommended for Canadian service businesses, tradies, freelancers)</strong></p>
      <ol style="margin:0.5rem 0; padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem;">
        <li>In <a href="/settings">Settings → How clients pay you</a>, set <strong>Default payment mode</strong> to <em>e-Transfer only</em></li>
        <li>Enter your e-Transfer email (e.g. <code>you@gmail.com</code>)</li>
        <li>Optionally add custom instructions (e.g. <em>"Please send e-Transfer with invoice number in the memo"</em>)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Your invoices will display clear e-Transfer instructions and a "Mark paid" button on your dashboard for when the payment clears. <strong>No Stripe needed, no transaction fees.</strong></p>

      <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;"><strong style="color:var(--ink);">Option B — Stripe card payments (recommended for US/UK/AU freelancers, e-commerce, anyone whose clients prefer cards)</strong></p>
      <ol style="margin:0.5rem 0; padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem;">
        <li>Sign up or log in at <a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dashboard.stripe.com</a></li>
        <li>Go to <a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Developers → API keys</a></li>
        <li>Copy your <strong>Secret key</strong> (starts with <code>sk_test_</code> or <code>sk_live_</code>)</li>
        <li>Paste it into <a href="/settings">Settings → Payments (Stripe) → Your key</a></li>
        <li>Set <strong>Default payment mode</strong> to <em>Stripe</em> (or <em>Both</em> if some clients pay by e-Transfer)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Once set, a "Pay now" button appears on your client-facing invoices. Stripe handles the payment — money goes directly to your Stripe account. <strong>Note:</strong> Start with a <code>sk_test_</code> key to test, switch to <code>sk_live_</code> for real payments.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;"><strong>Not sure?</strong> Start with <strong>Option A</strong> (e-Transfer) — it works for ~70% of Canadian small businesses, no setup beyond entering your email, and you can switch to Stripe later if you need to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step 5 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge optional">5</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Enable email sending <span class="optional-tag">optional</span></h3>
      <p>JustInvoice can email invoices directly to your clients. Emails are sent from a shared sender address — great for getting started quickly.</p>
      <p>Email sending is pre-configured on the hosted version. If you're self-hosting, set <code>RESEND_API_KEY</code> in your <code>.env</code> file (get a free key at <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">resend.com</a>).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step 6 -->
  <div class="setup-step">
    <div class="step-badge">6</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h3>Create your first invoice</h3>
      <p>Once your settings are saved:</p>
      <ol style="margin:0.5rem 0; padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem;">
        <li>Go to your <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a> and click <strong>New invoice</strong></li>
        <li>Enter your client's name and email</li>
        <li>Add one or more line items with descriptions, quantities, and prices</li>
        <li>Set issue and due dates, then hit <strong>Save</strong></li>
        <li>From the invoice view, either <strong>Email to client</strong> or copy the <strong>share link</strong></li>
      </ol>
      <p>Your client gets a clean, professional invoice page where they can download the PDF and (if you've set up Stripe) pay online.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="background:#f0f7ff; border-color:#bfdbfe;">
    <p style="margin:0; font-size:0.95rem;">
      <strong>That's it.</strong> Most freelancers are fully set up in under 5 minutes.
      If something's not working, check your <a href="/settings">Settings</a> page for status indicators on each feature.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="setup-footer">
    <a href="/">&larr; Back to home</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/signup">Create account</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/login">Log in</a>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
